BUG A2 — Option 2b logic missing when drug product > 10 g/day

Current: pipeline always Option 1. Vasopressin approved uses Option 2b 
(731.52 g/day drug product > 10 g).

Fix in EI calculation:
1. Compute total drug product daily mass:
   For injection/liquid: daily_volume_mL × density_g_per_mL
   For solid: sum of unit masses × doses_per_day
2. If drug_product_daily_mass_g > 10:
   → Option 2b: permitted concentration = PDE / drug_product_daily_mass_g
   → Compare each element's summed concentration across components to the 
     Option 2b permitted concentration
   → Threshold row = 30% of Option 2b permitted concentration
3. If ≤ 10 g/day:
   → Option 1 (existing behavior)
4. Report which option was applied in narrative.

Acceptance: Vasopressin (drug product mass > 10 g/day) → Option 2b applied, 
matches approved TSR framework.

