BUG A3 — "<30% of Perm Conc" / "meets Option 1" must yield ZERO

REVERSAL of prior logic. DRL convention (from approved Vasopressin TSR):
   "vendor declarations conservatively applied 30% of Option 1 limits. 
    Since results reported as <30% of Option-1 limits (qualitative 
    representation), A VALUE OF ZERO WAS USED in the risk assessment."

Fix in perm_conc_to_ppm() and process_pdf_to_json():
1. When observed_level / raw text matches:
   - "<30% of Perm. Conc." / "% of Permitted Concentration"
   - "meets Option 1" / "complies with Option 1" / "below Option 1"
   - "<30% Option 1" or similar qualitative-below-limit statements
   → concentration_value = 0.0
   → data_status = "below_option1_qualitative"
   → observed_level = full raw text (audit trail)
2. Do NOT compute 30% × Option 1. Do NOT populate any numeric value.
3. Only populate a numeric concentration when the CoA gives an explicit 
   measured number (e.g., "0.15 ppm", "285 ppb").

Remove: the perm_conc_to_ppm 30%×Option1 computation entirely. Replace 
with zero-emission for qualitative below-limit declarations.

Acceptance: Vasopressin Dextrose (all "<30% Perm Conc") → all elements 0.0. 
Table 4 totals = 0. Conclusion = compliant, no confirmatory testing.

